{
  "message": "I've analyzed the Spokes order system against Parcelly's requirements. Key mismatches: phone format (free text vs +48XXXXXXXXX), address (free text vs structured fields), weight (kg float vs grams integer with 25kg parcel limit), size (missing vs required A/B/C), postcode/city extraction, and status mapping. I'll add schemas for webhook registration and status events, define the register_webhook operation, add the shipment_status_changed webhook, create semantic mappings for statuses, record decisions for each mismatch with owners, and add consumer scenarios covering our edge cases (phone normalization, address parsing, weight conversion, pallet vs parcel, idempotency, webhook handling). I propose Spokes converts all data before calling Parcelly.",
  "patches": [
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/schemas/ShipmentStatusChanged",
      "value": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["event", "shipment_id", "reference", "status", "occurred_at"],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "event": { "type": "string", "enum": ["shipment.status_changed"] },
          "shipment_id": { "type": "string" },
          "reference": { "type": "string" },
          "status": { "type": "string", "enum": ["CREATED", "COLLECTED", "IN_TRANSIT", "DELIVERED", "RETURNED"] },
          "occurred_at": { "type": "string", "format": "date-time" }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/schemas/RegisterWebhookRequest",
      "value": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["url"],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "url": { "type": "string", "format": "uri" }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/schemas/RegisterWebhookResponse",
      "value": {
        "type": "object",
        "required": ["id", "url"],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "properties": {
          "id": { "type": "string" },
          "url": { "type": "string", "format": "uri" }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/operations/register_webhook",
      "value": {
        "description": "Register or replace the webhook endpoint for this partner",
        "direction": "consumer_to_provider",
        "request": {
          "method": "POST",
          "path": "/v1/webhooks",
          "headers": {
            "Authorization": { "required": true, "pattern": "^Bearer .+$" }
          },
          "body": { "$ref": "#/schemas/RegisterWebhookRequest" }
        },
        "responses": {
          "200": { "body": { "$ref": "#/schemas/RegisterWebhookResponse" } },
          "401": { "body": { "$ref": "#/schemas/Error" } },
          "400": { "body": { "$ref": "#/schemas/Error" } }
        },
        "stub": {
          "default_status": 200,
          "body": { "id": "wh_{{seq}}", "url": "{{request.body.url}}" }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/webhooks/shipment_status_changed",
      "value": {
        "description": "Parcelly notifies Spokes when a shipment status changes",
        "direction": "provider_to_consumer",
        "request": {
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "${CONSUMER_WEBHOOK_URL}",
          "headers": {
            "X-Parcelly-Signature": { "required": true, "pattern": "^sha256=[0-9a-f]{64}$" }
          },
          "body": { "$ref": "#/schemas/ShipmentStatusChanged" }
        },
        "signature": {
          "algorithm": "hmac-sha256",
          "header": "X-Parcelly-Signature",
          "format": "sha256={hex}",
          "over": "raw_body",
          "secret": "webhook_secret"
        },
        "consumer_responses": { "valid_signature": 200, "invalid_signature": 401 }
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/semantic_mappings/shipment_status_to_order_status",
      "value": {
        "CREATED": "paid",
        "COLLECTED": "shipped",
        "IN_TRANSIT": "shipped",
        "DELIVERED": "delivered",
        "RETURNED": "cancelled"
      }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": { "id": "D1", "text": "Spokes converts customer phone numbers from free-text Polish formats to Parcelly's required +48XXXXXXXXX (9 digits after +48) before calling create_shipment. Conversion strips spaces, dashes, parentheses, leading 0048/+48, and ensures exactly 9 digits after +48.", "owner": "consumer" }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": { "id": "D2", "text": "Spokes extracts postcode (NN-NNN), city, street, and building from the free-text address_line. If extraction fails (incomplete address), Spokes will not call create_shipment and will flag the order for warehouse callback.", "owner": "consumer" }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": { "id": "D3", "text": "Spokes converts order weight from kg (float, 3 decimals) to grams (integer) by multiplying by 1000 and rounding. If weight_g > 25000, Spokes calls the pallet endpoint (/v1/pallets) with pallet_type EUR; otherwise calls create_shipment with size determined by weight brackets (A ≤5000g, B 5001-15000g, C 15001-25000g).", "owner": "consumer" }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": { "id": "D4", "text": "Spokes uses its order ID (ORD-<number>) as the Idempotency-Key header for create_shipment. The key is ≤255 chars and scoped to our partner account. Blank key is treated as missing by Parcelly, so we always send it.", "owner": "consumer" }
    },
    {
      "op": "add",
      "path": "/decisions/-",
      "value": { "id": "D5", "text": "Spokes validates webhook signatures using HMAC-SHA256 over the raw request body with the shared webhook_secret. Invalid or missing signatures return 401; valid signatures return 200 and update order status per semantic_mappings.", "owner": "consumer" }
    },
    {
